      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling is a very common and valid response to the \"heat death\" or \"entropy\" of the universe, often described as the \"dark flow\" of nihilism. While the end of the universe may be true, the value of life often stems from the experience of being alive *now* rather than the outcome at the end of time. Many people find comfort in the \"connect and hope for the best\" approach, accepting the end to make the struggle precious.",
